### Design philosophy

See [docs/ENGINEERING_PHILOSOPHY.md](docs/ENGINEERING_PHILOSOPHY.md). Core idea: **bounded state**, **deterministic artifacts**, **inspection over orchestration**, **stabilization over expansion**. Complexity growth requires exceptional justification.

### Repository philosophy

[docs/REPOSITORY_STANDARDS.md](docs/REPOSITORY_STANDARDS.md): **repository consistency is preferred over tooling diversity.** Frozen runtime contracts, pinned dev tools (`requirements-dev.txt`), bounded lint scope.

### Reproducibility guarantees

| Guaranteed | Not guaranteed |
|------------|----------------|
| Artifact lifecycle order, filenames | `generated_at` timestamps |
| JSON `KEY_ORDER`, schema v1 | OpenAI / model outputs |
| Deterministic ZIP member order | Network / Telegram behavior |
| Contract tests in CI | Identical benchmark counters every nightly |

Details: [docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md](docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md) · [docs/examples/reproducible_runtime_workflow.md](docs/examples/reproducible_runtime_workflow.md)

### Quality workflow

```bash
make install-dev    # requirements.txt + requirements-dev.txt
make quality        # contracts → smoke → lint → format-check
make ci-test        # runtime → smoke → contracts (CI sections)
```

### CI expectations

GitHub Actions `Tests` workflow runs `make ci-test` (Python 3.12, pinned pytest). No matrix, no deploy stages. Optional local: `make lint` on `observability/`, `newsroom/`, `tests/contracts/`.

### Maintenance principles

- **Compatibility-first** — additive changes within 1.0.x; see [docs/MAINTENANCE_POLICY.md](docs/MAINTENANCE_POLICY.md).
- **New architectural layers require exceptional justification.**
- Do not add runtime artifacts or governance layers without ADR + contract updates.
- Before tagging: `make release-check` · [docs/RELEASE_FINALIZATION.md](docs/RELEASE_FINALIZATION.md).

### Supported operational model

- Single-node, SQLite-first, shell-first inspection (`make runtime-help`).
- Offline validation only — no enforcement daemons.
- Optional Redis/Postgres; documented degraded modes.

### Design principles

- **Deterministic tooling** — offline steps prefer stable JSON and explicit CLI contracts (`docs/RUNTIME_OPS.md`, `docs/CI_CD.md`).
- **Bounded state** — runtime JSON and artifacts are capped and pruned by design ([ADR-001](docs/architecture/ADR-001-bounded-runtime-state.md)).
- **Operational simplicity** — scripts and sequential wrappers instead of a control plane ([ADR-003](docs/architecture/ADR-003-no-orchestration-policy.md)).
- **Production-lite** — single-node realism: SQLite-first, optional Postgres/Redis, no mandatory SaaS stack ([`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`](docs/DEPLOYMENT.md)).
- **Composable operational layers** — each tool stands alone; `runtime_ops` only sequences calls.

### Deployment (production-lite)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.env.example` | Local dev template (safe placeholders) |
| `deploy/example.env.production-lite` | Single-node host / Compose template |
| `deploy/docker-compose.production-lite.yml` | Minimal Compose (one service, explicit runtime volume) |
| `deploy/systemd/newsroom-nightly.*` | Scheduled `make runtime-nightly` |
| `examples/runtime_samples/` | Sanitized demo JSON (no secrets) |

No Kubernetes, Helm, Terraform, Ansible, or in-repo deployment orchestrator.

### Runtime inspection flow

```bash
make runtime-help
make runtime-nightly RUNTIME_DIR=./var/runtime OUTPUT_DIR=./runtime_ops_output
make runtime-index OUTPUT_DIR=./runtime_ops_output
make verify-runtime OUTPUT_DIR=./runtime_ops_output
```

Gate releases: [docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md](docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md) · [docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md](docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md)

### Architecture maturity

- **Governance complete** — runtime contracts frozen; see [docs/architecture/RUNTIME_MATURITY.md](docs/architecture/RUNTIME_MATURITY.md).
- **Stabilization** — ADR-015; no new `runtime/*.json` artifact types planned.
- **Inspection-only** — policies describe assumptions, not enforcement daemons.

### Non-goals (documentation-level)

- No distributed orchestration for the editorial pipeline.
- No realtime telemetry platform as a hard dependency.
- No mandated microservice migration path.
- No infrastructure abstraction layer inside the app that hides deployment paths.
- No Kubernetes/Helm/Terraform/Ansible, autoscaling, service mesh, or web admin panel in-repo.
- No CI-driven production deployment automation (release discipline over deploy automation).

### Operational maturity (positioning)

- **Deterministic** offline checks: preflight, benchmark payload, soak simulation, artifact bundle, regression vs baseline, release qualification, static HTML dashboard, filesystem retention (`docs/RUNTIME_*.md`).
- **No orchestration engine** — sequential wrappers only (`tools/runtime_ops.py`).
- **Optional** Redis/Postgres; degraded modes are documented, not hidden.

### Runtime lifecycle (operational checks)

Text flow for bundles / CI / manual review (same logical order as `nightly-check`):

```
preflight
    ↓
runtime (live process: scheduler + bot + workers as configured)
    ↓
benchmark + soak
    ↓
artifact bundle (runtime_bundle.zip)
    ↓
regression (vs baseline bundle)
    ↓
qualification
    ↓
dashboard (static HTML)
    ↓
retention (artifact cleanup)
```

